# Review Notes

## Summary
T067 analysis support, evaluated hands-on by two agents,
fixed, and landed as four commits (221adde..e892f79).

## Observations
- Both evaluators confirmed the task closes: the slot rule
  was hand-derived on the fixtures (the old formula
  double-counted a slot, scoring 2/3 where the shared rule
  gives 1/2), write-once protects recorded bytes, and the
  support check rejects from all four entry points.
- One security blocker existed: verifyArtifactsOf joined
  manifest paths without validation and followed symlinks,
  turning study analyze into a file-existence and sha256
  oracle. The exposure pre-existed on main through the
  evaluate and compare handlers.
- Fix 21baecf: isSafeRelativePath gates every entry before
  any read, lstat refuses non-regular files, malformed
  entries are drift findings, and each batch manifest digest
  is anchored to its completion document before any evidence
  is read. Failing-first tests cover traversal, symlink,
  absolute-path, malformed-entry, and laundered-manifest
  probes.

## Verdict
Approved after fix. Full CI green on main. The same fix
heals the pre-existing oracle reachable through evaluate and
compare.
